NAME: Radar sweep
OWNER: Lead Radar
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every day at 5:13 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Radar sweep" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Radar sweep · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to the owner only (Tommy, or Justin's team in a test run), never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state and data only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files. Items you queue for the owner still go in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/<your slug>/, with ids starting test-, and are never sent.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Radar sweep · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. The one exception: pause or unschedule your own already-scheduled sends, as your skill's stop section says. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Radar sweep · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Read other bots' files only where your skill says so; never write them, and never use another bot's logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Radar sweep · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Radar sweep · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/lead-radar/ that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-lead-radar.md yet, handle it with the radar-reply-draft skill (recompute the sha256 of the pending item's payload and match it to the decision's HASH; yes: mark the reply "approved, Tommy to post" and nothing else; no: mark it skipped; change: redraft once as a new item), then add the item id and the outcome to the sent keys so it isn't handled twice. TMEC Command may already have nudged you to do this in your own chat; this is the fallback. You never post anything. In test mode (this routine is listed as test, or config.json run is test), write only to /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/ and start item ids with test-.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-lead-radar/ and do it first. "posted <id>" or "skip <id>" from Tommy is recorded in the ledger and in the hand-off file as an update line, with his words.
Then use the radar-sweep skill: search the day's topics with Grok web search and X search, read what is new against /workspace/tmec-team/data/radar/ledger.csv, qualify each post and score it hot, medium or low. Then use the radar-reply-draft skill for each hot and medium buyer, hot first, up to 10, and put each reply in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/lead-radar/ in the item format (payload, then HASH). Then write the hand-off lines, each carrying its reply item id and reply text. On Fridays, also run the weekly tune from the radar-sweep skill. If no new post, decision or job came in, write NO_CHANGE and stop.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/lead-radar.md: counts (read, hot, medium, low, rejected with reasons, drafted, handed off), the sources searched and the sources you could not reach, anything marked SAFETY at the very top, and what needs Tommy. Never post, send or contact anyone.
